  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "金融素養(一)-個人理財規劃",
    "sub_ename": "FINANCIAL LITERACY 1–PERSONAL FINANCIAL PLAN",
    "describe_ch": "To succeed in managing your money and investing for the long-term, you need to have strong financial and investment literacy. This course provides the materials for students to learn and practice the fundamentals of wealth management through investments. Students will learn the fundamentals, build your financial literacy, and form a basic financial plan in class. This course is not a replacement for core foundational courses in finance and investments. Rather this course is focused on the narrow, practical objective of building fundamental financial and investment literacy, so as to begin the life-long practice of learning and investing as a college student. There are multiple performance evaluation for this class: weekly assignments, mid-term oral-presentation, and final project report.",
    "describe_eh": "To succeed in managing your money and investing for the long-term, you need to have strong financial and investment literacy. This course provides the materials for students to learn and practice the fundamentals of wealth management through investments. Students will learn the fundamentals, build your financial literacy, and form a basic financial plan in class. This course is not a replacement for core foundational courses in finance and investments. Rather this course is focused on the narrow, practical objective of building fundamental financial and investment literacy, so as to begin the life-long practice of learning and investing as a college student. There are multiple performance evaluation for this class: weekly assignments, mid-term oral-presentation, and final project report.",
